{"genre": "Reuters", "passage_A": "In recent years, the growth of e-commerce has fundamentally altered how we conduct business and shop. Customers can now buy products from anywhere in the world with just a few clicks, while businesses can extend their reach beyond their local markets. Yet, alongside these benefits comes a challenge: navigating the myriad of regulations and boundaries that arise from globalization.

